<usx version="3.1">
<book code="2TH" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">2 Thessalonians</para>

<para style="toc1">2 Thessalonians</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2TH 1"/>

<para style="s">Greetings to the Thessalonians</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Thessalonians 1:1–10</char></note>Paul and Silvanus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Silas</char></note> and Timothy, </para>

<para style="p" vid="2TH 1:1">To the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ: <verse eid="2TH 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 1:2"/>Grace to you⁺ and peace from God our Father<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL, NE, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God the Father</char></note> and the Lord Jesus Christ. <verse eid="2TH 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 1:3"/>We ought to thank God always concerning you⁺, brothers, just as it is worthy, because your⁺ faith is growing exceedingly, and the love of each one of you⁺ all to one another is increasing, <verse eid="2TH 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 1:4"/>so as for us ourselves to boast in you⁺ in the churches of God for your⁺ endurance and faith in all your⁺ persecutions and in the tribulations that you⁺ are bearing, <verse eid="2TH 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 1:5"/>a plain token of the righteous judgment of God, for you⁺ to be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which also you⁺ suffer. <verse eid="2TH 1:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Christ’s Coming</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 1:6"/>For indeed <char style="add">it is</char> righteous with God to repay those oppressing you⁺ with tribulation, <verse eid="2TH 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 1:7"/>and to you⁺ being oppressed, relief with us at the revelation of the Lord Jesus from heaven with the angels of His power <verse eid="2TH 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 1:8"/>in a fire of flame, giving vengeance on those not knowing God and on those not obeying the gospel of our Lord Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ALT, HF, F35, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> <verse eid="2TH 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 1:9"/>who will pay the penalty of eternal destruction away from the presence of the Lord and from the glory of His power, <verse eid="2TH 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 1:10"/>when He shall come to be glorified in His saints and to be marveled at among all those having believed—because our testimony to you⁺ was believed—in that day. <verse eid="2TH 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 1:11"/>For <char style="add">this</char> also we pray always for you⁺, that our God may count you⁺ worthy of the calling and may fulfill every good pleasure of goodness and work of faith in power, <verse eid="2TH 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 1:12"/>so that the name of our Lord Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ALT, F35, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the name of our Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> may be glorified in you⁺, and you⁺ in Him, according to the grace of our God and of the Lord Jesus Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the grace of our God and Lord, Jesus Christ.</char></note> <verse eid="2TH 1:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="2TH 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2TH 2"/>

<para style="s">The Man of Lawlessness</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 2:1"/>Now we ask you⁺, brothers, on behalf of the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and of our gathering together unto Him, <verse eid="2TH 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 2:2"/>for you⁺ not quickly to be shaken in mind, nor to be alarmed, neither through spirit nor through word, nor through letter as through us, as that the day of the Lord<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the day of Christ</char></note> is present. <verse eid="2TH 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 2:3"/>Let no one deceive you⁺ in <char style="add">any</char> way, because <char style="add">it is</char> not unless the apostasy shall have come first, and the man of lawlessness<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the man of sin</char></note> shall have been revealed—the son of destruction, <verse eid="2TH 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 2:4"/>the one opposing and exalting himself above every so-called god or object of worship—so as for him to sit down in the temple of God,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as God</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> setting forth that he himself is God. <verse eid="2TH 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 2:5"/>Do you⁺ not remember that, being still with you⁺, I was saying these things to you⁺? <verse eid="2TH 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 2:6"/>And now you⁺ know what is restraining for him to be revealed in his own time. <verse eid="2TH 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 2:7"/>For the mystery of lawlessness is working already, only the one at present is restraining <char style="add">it</char> until he might be out of the midst. <verse eid="2TH 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 2:8"/>And then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord Jesus will slay<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">whom the Lord will consume</char></note> with the breath of His mouth and will annul by the appearing of His coming, <verse eid="2TH 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 2:9"/>whose coming is according to the working of Satan, in every power and in signs and in wonders of falsehood, <verse eid="2TH 2:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 2:10"/>and in every deception of wickedness to those perishing, because they did not receive the love of the truth in order for them to be saved. <verse eid="2TH 2:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 2:11"/>And because of this, God sends to them a working of delusion for them to believe the lie, <verse eid="2TH 2:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 2:12"/>so that all those not having believed the truth but having been well pleased in unrighteousness should be judged. <verse eid="2TH 2:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Stand Firm</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TH 2:13"/>But we ought to give thanks to God always concerning you⁺, brothers beloved by the Lord, because God chose you⁺ from the beginning<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God chose you as the firstfruits</char></note> unto salvation in the sanctification of the Spirit and belief of the truth, <verse eid="2TH 2:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TH 2:14"/>to which also He called you⁺ through our gospel to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ. <verse eid="2TH 2:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TH 2:15"/>So then, brothers, stand firm and hold fast to the traditions that you⁺ were taught, whether by word or by letter from us. <verse eid="2TH 2:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TH 2:16"/>Now our Lord Jesus Christ Himself and God our Father,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our God and Father</char></note> the One having loved us and having given <char style="add">us</char> eternal comfort and good hope in grace, <verse eid="2TH 2:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TH 2:17"/>may He comfort your⁺ hearts, and may He strengthen <char style="add">you</char> in every good work and word. <verse eid="2TH 2:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="2TH 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2TH 3"/>

<para style="s">Request for Prayer</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 3:1"/>Finally, brothers, pray for us that the word of the Lord may run and may be glorified, just as also with you⁺, <verse eid="2TH 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 3:2"/>and that we may be delivered from perverse and evil men; for the faith <char style="add">is</char> not unto all. <verse eid="2TH 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 3:3"/>But faithful is the Lord, who will strengthen you⁺ and guard <char style="add">you</char> from the evil one.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from evil</char></note> <verse eid="2TH 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 3:4"/>And we are persuaded in the Lord as to you⁺, that both you⁺ are doing and you⁺ will do what we command.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">what we command you</char></note> <verse eid="2TH 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 3:5"/>And may the Lord direct your⁺ hearts into the love of God and into the perseverance of Christ. <verse eid="2TH 3:5"/></para>

<para style="s">A Warning against Idleness</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 3:6"/>Now we command you⁺, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to withdraw yourselves from every brother walking in an unruly manner and not according to the tradition that you received<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they received</char></note> from us. <verse eid="2TH 3:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 3:7"/>For you⁺ yourselves know how it is necessary to imitate us, because we were not unruly among you⁺, <verse eid="2TH 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 3:8"/>nor did we eat bread from anyone without payment, but in labor and toil, working night and day in order not to be burdensome upon any of you⁺, <verse eid="2TH 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 3:9"/>not that we do not have authority, but so that we might give ourselves <char style="add">as</char> a pattern to you⁺ for you to imitate us. <verse eid="2TH 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 3:10"/>For even when we were with you⁺, we were commanding you⁺ this, that “if anyone is not willing to work, neither let him eat.” <verse eid="2TH 3:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 3:11"/>For we hear some are walking among you⁺ in an unruly manner, not working at all, but being busybodies. <verse eid="2TH 3:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 3:12"/>Now to such we command and exhort by our Lord Jesus Christ, that, working with quietness, they should eat their own bread. <verse eid="2TH 3:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TH 3:13"/>Now you⁺, brothers, should not grow weary <char style="add">in</char> well-doing. <verse eid="2TH 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TH 3:14"/>And if anyone does not obey our word through the letter, take note of this one not to mix with him, so that he may be ashamed. <verse eid="2TH 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TH 3:15"/>And do not deem <char style="add">him</char> as an enemy, but admonish <char style="add">him</char> as a brother. <verse eid="2TH 3:15"/></para>

<para style="s">Signature and Final Greetings1 Corinthians 16:19–24</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TH 3:16"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Colossians 4:15–18</char></note>Now may the Lord of peace Himself give to you⁺ peace through everything in every way. The Lord <char style="add">be</char> with all of you⁺. <verse eid="2TH 3:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TH 3:17"/>The greeting <char style="add">is</char> in my own hand—Paul, which is <char style="add">my</char> sign in every letter. In this way I write. <verse eid="2TH 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TH 3:18"/>The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ <char style="add">be</char> with all of you⁺.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen.</char></note> <verse eid="2TH 3:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="2TH 3"/>

</usx>
